# PROLOGUE — "Soundcheck", part 1: the Pink Wyvern.
# Canon: docs/STORY.md (Prologue). Tone: PG-13, funny first, true second.

@scene prologue.intro
# PLOT: Open the game on Proclamation Night; set the first objective.
# CHARACTER: Eddar is smart, funny, overlooked, and fine with it (mostly). The Ledger device starts.
@bgm wyvern_soundcheck
@card SOLACE BAY — PROCLAMATION NIGHT
NARRATOR: Tonight the Rubric names the Hero of Legend. Every bar in Solace Bay is open late.
NARRATOR: Every bar needs someone to mop it.
@cam focus eddar
EDDAR: Three cola puddles, one mop, forty minutes to doors.
EDDAR: And somewhere, a prophecy deciding whose life matters. Spoiler: not the guy holding the mop.
LEDGER: Entry #2,204: Mopped the stage at 6. Band spilled cola on the stage at 6:05. Mopped it at 6:10. Band asked why the stage was wet.
@objective Mop the three cola puddles before soundcheck.
@flag p.intro
@end

@scene prologue.puddle_1
# PLOT: Tutorial interaction. CHARACTER: Eddar's observational wit.
@sfx mop
EDDAR: Cola, lime, and something that glows. Spike's been mixing "tour drinks" again.
@flag p.puddle_1
@set puddles += 1
@if puddles>=3
EDDAR: Done. The floor is clean, the band is dirty, the universe is balanced.
@objective Find out why Roxy's amp keeps buzzing.
@endif
@end

@scene prologue.puddle_2
@sfx mop
EDDAR: This one's shaped like Rex's face. I'll take my time.
EDDAR: ...Okay, that was cathartic.
@flag p.puddle_2
@set puddles += 1
@if puddles>=3
EDDAR: Done. The floor is clean, the band is dirty, the universe is balanced.
@objective Find out why Roxy's amp keeps buzzing.
@endif
@end

@scene prologue.puddle_3
@sfx mop
EDDAR: Somebody tracked roller-skate wax through the cola. On purpose. Into a spiral.
EDDAR: That's not a spill. That's a signature.
LULU: Love you, Eddar!
@flag p.puddle_3
@set puddles += 1
@if puddles>=3
EDDAR: Done. The floor is clean, the band is dirty, the universe is balanced.
@objective Find out why Roxy's amp keeps buzzing.
@endif
@end

@scene prologue.roxy
# PLOT: Introduce Roxy and the amp problem. CHARACTER: her fuse, her ambition, her family; Eddar's crush.
@if p.amp_fixed
ROXY [smile]: Listen to that. Clean as a church bell. You're a wizard, Eddar.
EDDAR: I'm a guy who reads amp manuals for fun.
ROXY: Same thing in this town.
@end
@endif
@if p.amp_checked
ROXY [angry]: Well? Is she dying? Tell me she's not dying. I can't afford a new one. I can barely afford this ponytail.
EDDAR: Give me a second with it.
@end
@endif
@cam focus roxy
@sfx amp_buzz
ROXY [angry]: Do you hear that? That BZZZ? That's the sound of my career getting electrocuted.
EDDAR: It's a sixty-cycle hum. It's probably not personal.
ROXY [angry]: Everything is personal, Eddar. There's a booker from Amplitude in the crowd tonight. AMPLITUDE. If this thing buzzes through my solo, I'm going to set it on fire. And then the stage. And then myself.
@emote roxy fire
SPIKE: Her hair's doing the thing again.
ROXY [angry]: My hair is FINE.
? Offer to look at the amp. -> look
? Tell her the hair is a fire hazard. -> hazard {bond_roxy:-1}
? Ask about the booker. -> booker {bond_roxy:+1}
* booker
ROXY [smile]: Lady named Velvet Kane. Books the Grand Stadium. One good set and the Wildfires play Amplitude.
ROXY: Which means real money. Which means my brothers get shoes that fit before the next growth spurt.
EDDAR: Then the amp doesn't buzz tonight.
@goto look
* hazard
EDDAR: Respectfully, your hair is a fire hazard.
ROXY [angry]: Respectfully, so is your mouth. FIX. THE. AMP.
@goto look
* look
EDDAR: Let me look at it. Two minutes.
ROXY [smile]: You're my lucky charm, you know that?
LEDGER: Entry #2,205: "Lucky charm." Not "boyfriend material." Not "date." Charm. Like a rabbit's foot. Something you keep in your pocket and forget about.
@flag p.amp_checked
@objective Examine Roxy's amp, stage right.
@end

@scene prologue.amp
# PLOT: Small puzzle; Eddar's ear for the Resonance (foreshadows his power). CHARACTER: competence.
@if !p.amp_checked
EDDAR: Roxy's amp. "Property of Roxy Vega. Touch it and die." Fair enough. I'll ask first.
@end
@endif
@if p.amp_fixed
EDDAR: Purring like a cat that's eaten a smaller, louder cat.
@end
@endif
@sfx amp_buzz
EDDAR: Tubes glowing. Cables seated. The buzz is coming from... everywhere and nowhere.
NARRATOR: Eddar closes his eyes. Under the buzz there's a second sound, faint and low, like the room itself humming.
EDDAR: There. The hum isn't in the amp. It's in the ground. The stage lights and the amp are fighting over the same wire.
? Flip the ground-lift switch. -> lift {harmony:+1}
? Replace the power tube. -> tube
? Hit it. Percussive maintenance. -> hit
* tube
@sfx clunk
EDDAR: New tube. Same buzz. Two tokens' worth of glass, and the universe laughs at me.
@set tokens -= 2
EDDAR: Okay. Think. It's not the amp.
@goto retry
* hit
@sfx thump
EDDAR: ...
SPIKE: Did you just punch Roxy's amp?
EDDAR: No.
SPIKE: I'm telling her.
EDDAR: It was a diagnostic tap.
@goto retry
* retry
? Flip the ground-lift switch. -> lift {harmony:+1}
? Hit it again, but with feeling. -> hit2
* hit2
@sfx thump
NARRATOR: It still buzzes. Spike is writing something down.
@goto retry2
* retry2
? Flip the ground-lift switch. -> lift {harmony:+1}
* lift
@sfx switch
@bgm wyvern_live
NARRATOR: Click. The buzz dies. The room exhales.
EDDAR: Ground loop. Never personal. Always the ground.
@flag p.amp_fixed
@cam focus roxy
ROXY [smile]: Is that — oh, that's CLEAN. Listen to her!
@sfx guitar_riff
NARRATOR: Roxy hits one chord and the neon over the stage flares a little brighter, the way it does when someone in Solace Bay plays like they mean it.
ROXY [smile]: C'mere, lucky charm.
@emote roxy kiss
NARRATOR: She kisses him on the forehead.
LEDGER: Entry #2,206: Forehead. Again.
MAMA DEE: Eddar! Trash. Alley. Now. Before the doors open and the whole Bay smells my kitchen.
@objective Take the trash out the back door.
@end

@scene prologue.mama_dee
# CHARACTER: Mama Dee — owner, gravel voice, secretly the only adult who looks out for Eddar.
@if p.amp_fixed
MAMA DEE: Trash, sugar. Back door. And if Rex Valor's out there, you walk past him like he's weather.
EDDAR: Weather doesn't usually stuff me in a barrel.
MAMA DEE: Then you ain't seen weather in Solace Bay.
@end
@endif
MAMA DEE: You know what tonight is, Eddar? The Rubric reads out a name and some lucky fool becomes a legend.
EDDAR: Any chance it's the guy who mops?
MAMA DEE: Honey, prophecy don't mop. That's why it needs us.
@if puddles<3
MAMA DEE: Floor. Cola. Go.
@endif
@end

@scene prologue.spike
@if p.amp_fixed
SPIKE: I didn't tell her you punched the amp. I want that on the record. I'm holding it over you for life.
@end
@endif
SPIKE: Bass player life: nobody hears you, everybody would notice if you stopped. Kind of like you, mop guy.
EDDAR: That's the nicest thing you've ever said to me.
SPIKE: Don't get used to it.
@end

@scene prologue.lulu
@if p.amp_fixed
LULU: Roxy's playing like the building owes her money. Good job, Eddar.
@end
@endif
LULU: I'm warming up. Don't talk to me. Actually, talk to me. Did you see the Proclamation scroll? They say the ink glows red when it picks the Hero.
EDDAR: I've read the Canticle. Twice. The Hero verse doesn't even scan.
LULU: You've READ it? The whole thing? On purpose?
EDDAR: I clean the Hall of Records at night. It was that or talk to the ghosts.
@end

@scene prologue.gil
# CHARACTER: barfly with a micro-story. Plants Sable's arrival.
GIL: Saw a woman ride in on a black light-cycle this afternoon. Visor. Silver hair. Didn't stop at the Proclamation tent.
GIL: Didn't stop anywhere. Just looked at every face on the boardwalk like she was reading a list.
EDDAR: Looking for someone?
GIL: Kid, everybody's looking for someone. Most of us are just looking for the bathroom.
@end

@scene prologue.jukebox
@if p.amp_fixed
EDDAR: Someone queued "Valor Forever (Demo)" four times. Rex has been here.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: Mama Dee's jukebox. Every record is from before I was born, except for the one I fixed. I won't say which one. It knows.
@end

@scene prologue.front_door
EDDAR: Front door's locked until doors. Mama Dee's rule: nobody in until the floor's clean, and nobody out until the trash is.
@end

@scene prologue.back_door_locked
EDDAR: The alley can wait. Soundcheck first, says the woman who signs my paychecks.
@end
